{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458812-what-if","id":1458812,"title":"What If ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-05T04:56:07-07:00","id":1458812,"title":"What If ?","content":"What if all the Antediluvians died in a certain way around the year -0-. (There is no doubt, they are truly dead)<br /> <br /> There could still be a rebellion against the elders leading to the establishing of the Camarilla and the Anarchs /Sabbat. Or would they only be anarchs and no Sabbat?<br /> The Sabbat would no longer be against the antediluvians but that could quickly become against ancient vampires (methuselahs? Would they claim to rebel against Cain?<br /> The Tremere would not diablerize Saulot and would not have an antediluvian. Would they have survived? <br /> The Giovanni would not have diablerized Cappadocian but some Capadoccian methuselahs. Would they have survived and thrived?<br /> Would the Leaders of the sects behave differently knowing there is no threat of those ancient monsters awakening?<br /> <br /> How would the world of darkness be if vampires didn't have this threat having above their heads?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T05:34:15-07:00","id":1458814,"title":"","content":"Sabbat would likely have formed anyway based around the Ritae, Vinculum being still the most important, and they would rebel and war against the Elders who ruled through bloodbonds and against the Camarilla which is an organization of Elder puppets (as far as the Sabbat is conserned).<br /> <br /> Tremere would likely still survive though they might have had a rougher but even without an Antediluvian they still had Mastery of Blood magics to offer in exchange of alliances formed.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni would have diablerized Cappadocian Methuselahs but they might not have such a clear victory over them. I would say they would survive but their war against the Cappadocians could drag on for centuries.<br /> <br /> Camarilla leaders would act as they always have, securing their and being pro-Elder ivory tower.<br /> Sabbats war would likely be less urgent and due to that they might act less openly than bow and undermine Camarilla rule through more insidious ways, likely trying to convert and turn Camarilla neonates to turn on their elders.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness would be just as bleak and hopeless even without the Antediluvian threat.<br /> <br /> Above are only my personal opinions on the matter YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T05:36:06-07:00","id":1458815,"title":"","content":"Setites would likely be more at loss without their Dark God and the possibility of his ascension, though religions generally have no need for proof so even that might work out the same in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T07:58:01-07:00","id":1458834,"title":"","content":"I suspect Methuselahs would just take the top spot and the often torpid but always reclusive masters of the Jyhad. It\u2019s easy to miss because they actually have listed caps instead of ??? for their generation entries, but entire arrays of elder powers up to the 9 dot varieties and 9 dots in attributes and abilities is pretty game breakingly powerful.<br /> <br /> Hell, a Methuselah with all the common disciples at only 5 dots and a convenient blood supply could have more global influence than any player would know what to do with.<br /> <br /> My own personal headcanon (coming from BJD where one option for the sarcophagus is a lucid Ynoch who admits the Antediluvians are not as powerful as they pretend to be) for games I run is that vampiric power caps at 4th Gen (and all the generations will eventually; as in millennia; thicken to the same plateau) and the only difference between the Antediluvians and Methuselahs is a bigger spent XP total.<br /> <br /> In my current campaign Tremere was the first modern vampire to realize this secret, which is why he was willing to give up on his 3rd Gen body to take possession of Goratrix\u2019s 4th Gen one... it wasn\u2019t actually the debuff everyone thinks it was, he just wants everyone to think it is so they\u2019ll underestimate him. The plateau coupled with thickening blood also leaves open the possibility that Caine wasn\u2019t the actual first vampire, just the first one recorded in the line the antediluvians and their descendants trace their ancestry through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T08:23:44-07:00","id":1458838,"title":"","content":"How much of the game really lingers on the objective truth of the Antedilluvians? For most of the game it could well be just a legend or they could have all died before the Greeks had a writing system.<br /> <br /> You may take this in two ways. One is that their demise is a certainty for the players, but can't be proven to the characters (most likely). The other is that somehow it is proven beyond fair doubt that they existed but died, so believing in then is less like Christianity and more like Flat Earth.<br /> <br /> On the first take little to nothing changes. Almost nothing was really predicated on the Antedilluvians existing and even the newcomers that diablerized some Ancients wouldn't change a lot if they didn't. Tremere and Giovanni weren't leaders because of generation and the diablerie actually weakened their contact with their respective clans, as Tremere went into torpor and Augustus obsessed even more with the Underworld. The diablerie of Antedilluvians was far more symbolic than anything in the formation of Sabbat, and they are the original Anarchs, far more preoccupied with their Elders. Fighting the Ancients was more of a religious theme than anything the Time of Judgement. And the Setites are a cult that don't even believe in the Noddist doctrine, believing Set was either 2nd gen, 1st gen, God or whatever.<br /> <br /> Now, if even Setites must deal with the fact that Set is dead, or go full Flat Earth wacko, that can change... a few things, but just a few. The Sabbat must tinker a little more with their religion, but not a lot. More focus on god and less apocalyptic tone. Well, still apocalyptic, but in the original sense. Same package, same content, but some changes in text in the gift card. The Camarilla would have an easier time convincing neonates that Gehenna is a silly superstition because Gehenna IS a silly superstition. The Setites would probably split even more, with most focusing more in the Gnostic aspects of their religion and taking Set more as an Exemplar, but a few would form a cult even more obsessively dedicated to finding and resurrecting their god, similar to some Protestant extremists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T00:54:24-07:00","id":1458962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458812-what-if?p=1458834#post1458834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own personal headcanon (coming from BJD where one option for the sarcophagus is a lucid Ynoch who admits the Antediluvians are not as powerful as they pretend to be) for games I run is that vampiric power caps at 4th Gen (and all the generations will eventually; as in millennia; thicken to the same plateau) and the only difference between the Antediluvians and Methuselahs is a bigger spent XP total.<br /> <br /> In my current campaign Tremere was the first modern vampire to realize this secret, which is why he was willing to give up on his 3rd Gen body to take possession of Goratrix\u2019s 4th Gen one... it wasn\u2019t actually the debuff everyone thinks it was, he just wants everyone to think it is so they\u2019ll underestimate him. The plateau coupled with thickening blood also leaves open the possibility that Caine wasn\u2019t the actual first vampire, just the first one recorded in the line the antediluvians and their descendants trace their ancestry through.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the implications that idea would have for Augustus Giovanni; he thinks he's flubbed eating all of Cappadocius and is in a tizzy looking for the True Vessel because he <i>should be </i>more powerful, but doesn't realize he didn't screw up (or if he did, finishing the job wouldn't really gain him anything).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T02:42:06-07:00","id":1458976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458812-what-if?p=1458962#post1458962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the implications that idea would have for Augustus Giovanni; he thinks he's flubbed eating all of Cappadocius and is in a tizzy looking for the True Vessel because he <i>should be </i>more powerful, but doesn't realize he didn't screw up (or if he did, finishing the job wouldn't really gain him anything).</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re getting it.<br /> <br /> The plateau is also something the Antediluvians are desperate to hide (basically their invincibility is a bluff to keep themselves from being murdered the way they murdered their sires. It\u2019s also why so many Antediluvians are looking for ways to transcend the vampiric tradition because that\u2019s the only thing that would give them a real edge over the other antediluvians and methuselahs (while selling that the ticket for methuselahs is just to diablerize up to third so they don\u2019t go looking at alternative paths of power).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a masquerade within the masquerade sold by the present time of massively thinned out blood (the majority lack the ability to even use elder disciplines and their potential with attributes and abilities is no greater than a mortal), the methuselahs\u2019 memories of the times they were weaker than the antediluvians (before their blood fully thickened) and that 9 dot disciplines are already stupidly OP (take a look at what Chimerstry, Fortitude and Animalism 9 and then another look at what Ravnos actually did during the Week of Nightmares) and more xp gives them more of those 9 dot traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T07:08:55-07:00","id":1459005,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why the fourth generation Augustus Giovanni (who in this scenario is the top of the food chain already) would feel the need to war with his fellow Cappadocians. His will is so strong it creates a Giovanni Blood Line instead of Premascines being made by him pre eating of Cappadocious, all his Childer would have his clan flaw.<br /> <br /> I also see no reason for him to go to war as no one is shocked and angered by Cappadocious death. The Giovanni are most likely an accepted bloodline as the other Cappadocian off shoots are, with the advantage of being lead by a member of the fourth gen. Augustus might actually frown on his personal 5th gen Childer lowering their generation to 4th and becoming a clear rival to him. I think they just become a powerful faction of a powerful whole, the Cappadocian like their bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T08:30:52-07:00","id":1459011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458812-what-if?p=1459005#post1459005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why the fourth generation Augustus Giovanni (who in this scenario is the top of the food chain already) would feel the need to war with his fellow Cappadocians. His will is so strong it creates a Giovanni Blood Line instead of Premascines being made by him pre eating of Cappadocious, all his Childer would have his clan flaw.<br /> <br /> I also see no reason for him to go to war as no one is shocked and angered by Cappadocious death. The Giovanni are most likely an accepted bloodline as the other Cappadocian off shoots are, with the advantage of being lead by a member of the fourth gen. Augustus might actually frown on his personal 5th gen Childer lowering their generation to 4th and becoming a clear rival to him. I think they just become a powerful faction of a powerful whole, the Cappadocian like their bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually genuinely like this idea. It would change dynamics quite a lot if suddenly there were a Cappadocian clan which had survived. Would they be members of the Camarilla since the Cappadocians were a high clan? Would the same have happened to the Tremere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T08:34:00-07:00","id":1459013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458812-what-if?p=1458834#post1458834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my current campaign Tremere was the first modern vampire to realize this secret, which is why he was willing to give up on his 3rd Gen body to take possession of Goratrix\u2019s 4th Gen one... it wasn\u2019t actually the debuff everyone thinks it was, he just wants everyone to think it is so they\u2019ll underestimate him. The plateau coupled with thickening blood also leaves open the possibility that Caine wasn\u2019t the actual first vampire, just the first one recorded in the line the antediluvians and their descendants trace their ancestry through.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am warming up to this idea of a masquerade within the masquerade. It would even streamline the Kuei-jin if one would be so obliged as an offshoot of an ancestor of Caine. That would shake things up quite a lot though.<br /> <br /> So traits and disciplines stay at 9? or is it only disciplines and the rest can go to 10 (which is an improvement over 9, but nothing spectacular) and how do you do bloodpool and spend per round (same?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T08:36:08-07:00","id":1459014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458812-what-if?p=1458815#post1458815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setites would likely be more at loss without their Dark God and the possibility of his ascension, though religions generally have no need for proof so even that might work out the same in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Settites might indeed be hit hard since their source of &quot;faith&quot; disappears. But they might also go the, &quot;we'll resurrect him&quot; path!<br /> Which leaves me to wonder how the second fanatics (the Assamites) would change if their progenitor wasn't around any more? How would his Herald handle his disappearance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26925-denstoffy","name":"Denstoffy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T09:26:59-07:00","id":1459020,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458812-what-if?p=1458815#post1458815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setites would likely be more at loss without their Dark God and the possibility of his ascension, though religions generally have no need for proof so even that might work out the same in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, they kinda lost him tho' in the &quot;canon time line&quot;<br /> In 33.AD <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\">Set briefly awakened and made roughly 300 prophesies before returning to slumber, awakened for a brief time, covering the noonday sun in darkness. He was restless for three to seven nights, giving commandments and prophecies to his childer across the world, including telling them he will return in the future. The night after his voice falls silent, members of the Council of Tanis visit his hidden tomb and find his sarcophagus shattered, seemingly from the inside. Set is not heard from again.<br /> <br /> And... actually nobody knows whats happened with him, even some Gehenna scennarios were vague (in most of them he was in Duat) , tho' the Jyhad Diary made him a candidate for the inmate of the Sarchopagus...<br /> It is a bit funny to think about, there was a certain somebody who died in the same time...</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T12:15:03-07:00","id":1459042,"title":"","content":"Set appearing in 33 AD, performing signs and wonders, delivering prophecies, the eclipse, and the empty tomb all crib so blatantly from Gospel accounts of the Crucifixion of Jesus that I read that particular Setite legend as a heretical Gnostic cult thing that probably dates no further back than the adoption of Christianity as a state religion by the Romans in the early fourth century. Casting Set as Jesus might have seen use as some kind of big mystery school reveal to impress initiates who earned the Embrace.<br /> <br /> As for whose clan history changes the most in our dead Antedeluvian scenario, I believe the Cappadocians take the prize. They never suffer the Feast of Folly. Augustus Giovanni is born into a world where the Cappadocians are much more numerous, much more ideologically diverse, and where the ancient who wanted to embrace him in the canon timeline is long dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 09-06-2021, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T15:05:05-07:00","id":1459072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Denstoffy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458812-what-if?p=1459013#post1459013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am warming up to this idea of a masquerade within the masquerade. It would even streamline the Kuei-jin if one would be so obliged as an offshoot of an ancestor of Caine. That would shake things up quite a lot though.<br /> <br /> So traits and disciplines stay at 9? or is it only disciplines and the rest can go to 10 (which is an improvement over 9, but nothing spectacular) and how do you do bloodpool and spend per round (same?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally just use the limits for 4th Gen (9\u2019s for traits, 50/10 BP), but with the sheer amount of xp (or maturation points if you\u2019re using that system) that a 14,000+ year old pre-deluge vampire has over a 4000-5000 year old vampire basically gives a true Antediluvian 9\u2019s in multiple attributes, abilities and disciplines.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting is that, given how many have their own clan-defining disciplines (ex. Gangrel/Protean, Ravnos/Chimerstry, Lasombra/Obtenebration, Tzmisce/Vicissitude), I\u2019d argue that some form blood sorcery is common to many of the true Antediluvians as well (on the theory that all disciplines are offshoots of the blood sorcery Caine learned from Lilith* that got regimented and it\u2019s use normalized) and that gives them an edge as well.<br /> <br /> As to such a seemingly small blood pool of just 50; even 8th Gen elders have blood bound, dominated and duped guards they could feed from in emergency. A 3rd gen presumably has an assortment of dominated fresh methuselahs they create simply to fatten up and then feed from as needed and then kill before they can become bound.<br /> <br /> Ravnos during his rampage had countless supernaturals to feed from as they tried futilely to stop him. Werewolf blood is twice as potent as human blood, so that\u2019s 3x2=6 BP/turn sucked out of one to recharge itself. A 6th Gen has 3x the potence of human blood by volume so 9 BP per turn.<br /> <br /> Basically, an Antediluvian on the warpath has plenty of blood to fuel itself... and fueling itself also removes opponents at the same time. An Antediluvian NOT on the warpath who\u2019s active rather than using high level Auspex and other disciplines from torpor will also presumably have entire cults devoted to keeping itself fed.<br /> <br /> And yes, in my world the Wan-Kuei (i.e. the \u201ckuei-jin\u201d) are an offshoot of a 2nd Gen sired by Blood Caine before Caine** returned to found the First City. This ancient in turn sired its own 3rd Generation who became the mythical Yama Kings*** (the gist is that the servants of the Yama Kings and the Wan-Kuei are essentially sects... the servants seek out particularly wicked mortals, manipulate events to bring about their deaths and then give them the Second Breath/Embrace... the Wan-Kuei are a sect that doesn\u2019t embrace and only adopts those they can rescue from the servants of the Yama Kings. Their Dharmas are essentially means of achieving what\u2019s known in the West as Golconda (which is why those who reach high ranks can transcend generational limits just as those in Golconda can).<br /> <br /> * I particularly like this take because its roughly in line with the origin of Dracula\u2019s supernatural powers in Bram Stoker\u2019s novel; his magic powers were the result of learning the black arts from a hidden school (called Scholomance) supposedly run by Satan himself. Caine being instructed in blood magic by Lilith (a demon in most Middle Eastern myths) is a nice echo of how it worked for THE vampire who basically established all the modern tropes.<br /> <br /> ** Blood Caine is my shorthand for the actual first vampire in the same way humanity\u2019s earliest female common ancestor is called \u201cMitochondrial Eve.\u201d They may or may not be Biblical Caine (i.e. the vampire the western Kindred count their generations from) or even male, but since no one living has even seen them and we have to call them something \u201cCaine\u201d is as good a name as any. Regardless, the embrace of the common ancestor of the Wan-Kuei occurred prior to Biblical Caine\u2019s founding of the First City.<br /> <br /> *** While the Western Kindred diversified into distinctive clans, the Yama Kings did not... they are all effectively \u201cclanless\u201d in that there are no obvious characteristics that set the line of one Yama King from another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T15:27:44-07:00","id":1459073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458812-what-if?p=1459005#post1459005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why the fourth generation Augustus Giovanni (who in this scenario is the top of the food chain already) would feel the need to war with his fellow Cappadocians. His will is so strong it creates a Giovanni Blood Line instead of Premascines being made by him pre eating of Cappadocious, all his Childer would have his clan flaw.<br /> <br /> I also see no reason for him to go to war as no one is shocked and angered by Cappadocious death. The Giovanni are most likely an accepted bloodline as the other Cappadocian off shoots are, with the advantage of being lead by a member of the fourth gen. Augustus might actually frown on his personal 5th gen Childer lowering their generation to 4th and becoming a clear rival to him. I think they just become a powerful faction of a powerful whole, the Cappadocian like their bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting interpretation, and probably I'll use, and many here seem so inclined, too.<br /> <br /> But strictly speaking not even the Giovanni history need to change due to a lack of Antedilluvians. Giovanni was never Embraced directly by Cappadocius, anyway, instead he was taken by two of the oldest Childer of Cappadocius, with whom he had negotiated the deal, was drained and fed Cappadocius blood from a vial. The Antedilluvian himself plays a minor and unnecessary role by providing the vial, that could have happened a long time before. The Feast of Folly is before his Embrace and may have either happened before Cappadocius demise or by the hand of his eldest Childe instead. It changes very little either way.<br /> <br /> Finally, even though the current story says that Giovanni changed Clan Weakness after diablerizing Cappadocius, this is also unnecessary, since his lineage was kind of a separate cult and bloodline inside the clan already, keeping to themselves for more than 400 years before the coup. Plenty of time to change weakness and start the modern Giovanni.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}